## Measurement

Five legs, all on port1.0.48, all captured at frame level, all in one window.
**`dot1x initialize interface port1.0.48` was sent on the DUT before EVERY leg** (run 1's
lesson: a superseded EAP session's response is rejected by the NAS and the leg fails for a
reason that has nothing to do with the thing being tested).

### What the credential actually contains — measured, not assumed

A new generic helper, **`tools/p12split.py`**, splits a PKCS#12 and prints the DER size of
every certificate in it, so the client's flight size is arithmetic instead of a guess:

```
$ tools/tb tool tb277 t9032r2 p12split /tftproot/cktls.p12 --passwd ckbench2026 \
      --out-dir /tmp/t9032r2 --name cktls
bundle: /tftproot/cktls.p12
  LEAF    867 bytes DER  subject=O = AlliedWare Plus, CN = cktls
                        issuer =O = "Allied Telesis, Inc.", CN = AlliedWarePlusCAA2WQS700B  notAfter=Oct 22 01:35:41 2031 GMT
  CA[0]   874 bytes DER  subject=O = "Allied Telesis, Inc.", CN = AlliedWarePlusCAA2WQS700B
                        issuer =O = "Allied Telesis, Inc.", CN = AlliedWarePlusCAA2WQS700B  notAfter=Oct 14 06:32:24 2031 GMT
  predicted TLS Certificate payload: leaf-only 876 bytes, whole chain 1753 bytes
wrote:
  client_cert  /tmp/t9032r2/cktls-leaf.pem
  private_key  /tmp/t9032r2/cktls-key.pem   (mode 0600)
  chain (record only, NOT for client_cert)  /tmp/t9032r2/cktls-chain.pem
```

**Run 1's premise is confirmed:** the DUT's PKCS#12 does carry the issuing CA (874 bytes DER)
beside the leaf (867 bytes DER). The leaf is issued by `AlliedWarePlusCAA2WQS700B` — this very
unit's serial inside the CN — so the credential demonstrably came from this DUT.

### The five legs

| leg | credential | supplicant TLS | client flight | fragments | result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **R2-A** | whole PKCS#12 (leaf **+** CA) | 1.3 (default) | **2141 B** | **2**, flags `0xc0 LM` | timeout — stall reproduced |
| **R2-B** | leaf-only `client_cert` + `private_key`, **`ca_cert` = DUT CA** | 1.3 (default) | **2141 B** | **2**, flags `0xc0 LM` | timeout — **the hypothesis as written did NOT work** |
| **R2-C** | leaf-only, **no `ca_cert`** | 1.3 (default) | **1262 B** | **1**, flags `0x00` | timeout — fragmentation fixed, **still no conclusion** |
| **R2-D** | leaf-only, `ca_cert` = DUT CA | **1.2** (capped) | **2154 B** | **2**, flags `0xc0 LM` | 🟢 **EAP-Success at 1.0471 s, port Authorized** |
| **R2-E** | **control:** a certificate the DUT's CA did not issue | **1.2** (capped) | 1239 B | 1 | 🟢 **EAP-Failure at 1.0363 s, port Unauthorized** |

**For every leg the tool's `--json` file was checked against its printed RESULT** (run 1 saw
